{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.q_ns_wellposedness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.q_ns_wellposedness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp","lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.q_ns_energy_and_decay"],"declarations":32,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.q_ns_wellposedness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.q_ns_wellposedness","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L212-L238","doc":"**Global regularity of the q-deformed Navier--Stokes equation**\n([`thm:q-ns-wellposedness`]).\n\nThe block's full claim, assembled.  Existence, uniqueness and\nsmoothness are the class's open inputs; the energy inequality and the\nspectral decay are the two theorems above, and are **derived** from\nthe equations rather than assumed.\n\nThis is a conditional theorem in the §3b-cond sense and is honest\nabout which conjunct carries the open problem — unlike the previous\nencoding, in which every conjunct was assumed at once. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:q-ns-wellposedness","label":"thm:q-ns-wellposedness","md":"quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-ns-wellposedness.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.q_ns_spectral_decay","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.q_ns_spectral_decay","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L191-L210","doc":"**`Δ_q`-spectral decay** ([`thm:q-ns-wellposedness`] property (iii)):\n`|v̂_k(t)| ≤ |v̂_k(0)| · exp(−ν_q [k]_q² t)`.\n\n**Proved**, from the modal differential inequality — not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.q_ns_energy_inequality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.q_ns_energy_inequality","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L166-L189","doc":"**Energy inequality** ([`thm:q-ns-wellposedness`] property (ii)):\n`‖v(t)‖_A² + 2ν_q ∫₀ᵗ ‖d_q v(s)‖_A² ds ≤ ‖v₀‖_A²`.\n\n**Proved**, from the pointwise energy balance — not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.modal_inequality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.modal_inequality","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L162-L162","doc":"**THE EQUATION** (modal inequality): `Δ_q` acts on the `k`-th\neigenspace by `[k]_q²`, so the eigencomponent obeys\n`d/dt |v̂_k| ≤ −ν_q [k]_q² |v̂_k|`.  Again a statement about the\nrate; the exponential bound is derived in\n`q_ns_spectral_decay`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.modal_hasDeriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.modal_hasDeriv","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L154-L154","doc":"Each eigencomponent differentiates to its modal rate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.modal_continuousOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.modal_continuousOn","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L151-L151","doc":"Analytic regularity of each eigencomponent along a solution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.energy_balance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.energy_balance","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L147-L147","doc":"**THE EQUATION** (energy balance): the differential form of the\nq-NS energy identity.  Note this is a statement about the *rates*,\ni.e. about the equations — not about the integrated bound, which\nis derived from it in `q_ns_energy_inequality`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.energy_hasDeriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.energy_hasDeriv","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L137-L137","doc":"The energy functional differentiates to the sum of its rates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.energy_continuousOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.energy_continuousOn","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L132-L132","doc":"Analytic regularity of the energy functional along a solution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.dissipation_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.dissipation_zero","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L129-L129","doc":"Cumulative dissipation vanishes at `t = 0` (it is an integral\nfrom `0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.initial_datum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.initial_datum","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L126-L126","doc":"A solution starts at the initial datum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.smooth_of_isSolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.smooth_of_isSolution","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L124-L124","doc":"**OPEN INPUT.**  Interior regularity: a solution is smooth in the\ninternal hom of `𝐂`.  Block property (i). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.existence_uniqueness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.existence_uniqueness","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L120-L120","doc":"**OPEN INPUT.**  Global existence and uniqueness of the q-NS\nsolution.  This is the Millennium-adjacent content of the block\nand the only substantive thing assumed here (with\n`smooth_of_isSolution`).  Bean `qou-t28w`, tier B. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.modalRate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.modalRate","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L114-L114","doc":"Rate of change of the `k`-th eigencomponent magnitude. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.dissipationRate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.dissipationRate","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L112-L112","doc":"Instantaneous dissipation `D(t) = ‖d_q v(t)‖_A²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.energyRate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.energyRate","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L110-L110","doc":"Rate of change of the kinetic energy along a trajectory, `E'(t)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.IsSolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.IsSolution","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L108-L108","doc":"Solution predicate.  Opaque *definition* data — which trajectories\ncount as solutions — not an assumption that one exists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.Smooth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.Smooth","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L105-L105","doc":"Smoothness predicate.  Opaque *definition* data — which\ntrajectories count as smooth — not an assumption that any\ntrajectory is smooth. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.q_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.q_int","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L101-L101","doc":"The q-integer `[k]_q`; `Δ_q|_{V_k} = [k]_q² id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.v_hat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.v_hat","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L99-L99","doc":"The `k`-th `Δ_q`-eigencomponent magnitude `|v̂_k|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.dissipation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.dissipation","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L97-L97","doc":"Cumulative dissipation `t ↦ ∫₀ᵗ ‖d_q v(s)‖_A² ds`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.norm_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.norm_sq","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L95-L95","doc":"Squared Frobenius (`L²`) norm `‖·‖_A²` on velocities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.v₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.v₀","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L93-L93","doc":"The divergence-free initial velocity `v₀` (finite Frobenius norm). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.Pressure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.Pressure","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L91-L91","doc":"Carrier of pressures (elements of the algebra `A`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.Velocity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.Velocity","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L89-L89","doc":"Carrier of divergence-free velocity 1-forms `ker(δ_q|_{Ω¹(A)})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.ν_q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.ν_q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.ν_q_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.ν_q_eq","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L86-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.ν_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.ν_q","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L85-L85","doc":"The kinematic viscosity `ν_q = ½(1 − q⁻¹) > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.q","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L82-L82","doc":"The substrate parameter `q : ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L80-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QNsWellposednessContext","kind":"class","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_wellposedness.lean#L64-L164","doc":"Carrier data and hypotheses for [`thm:q-ns-wellposedness`].\n\nThe fields split into three kinds, and the split is the point:\n\n* **data** — carriers, the initial datum, the norm / dissipation /\n  eigencomponent functionals, the rate functionals, and the opaque\n  `Smooth` / `IsSolution` *predicates* (which fix what the words\n  mean, and assert nothing);\n* **the equations** — `energy_balance` and `modal_inequality`, the\n  pointwise differential statements the q-NS system makes, plus the\n  analytic regularity needed to integrate them;\n* **the open inputs** — `existence_uniqueness` and\n  `smooth_of_isSolution`, and nothing else.\n\nNeither the energy inequality nor the spectral-decay bound appears\nas a field; both are theorems below. ","signatureChunk":0}]}